  "poe": {
    "budgetW": 370,
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.fortinet.com/content/dam/fortinet/assets/data-sheets/pdf/fortiswitch-secure-access-series.pdf",
    "note": "24 PoE ports (ports 1-24), 370 W total. 370 W is 24 x 15.4 W, so all 24 PoE ports can power a Class 3 (802.3af) device but only twelve can power a Class 4 (802.3at, 30 W) device: 24 x 30 W = 720 W is not available. Internal AC supply, 100-240 V, 7 A max, 474.8 W average / 476.3 W maximum consumption."
  },
  "fabric": {
    "capacityMbps": 176000,
    "kind": "switching fabric",
    "note": "Datasheet switching capacity 176 Gbps duplex with 260 Mpps: 48x 1G plus 4x 10G is 88 Gbit/s of line rate, doubled to 176 Gbps full duplex."
  },
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.fortinet.com/content/dam/fortinet/assets/data-sheets/pdf/fortiswitch-secure-access-series.pdf",
  "notes": "Datasheet: 48x GE RJ45 and 4x 10GE SFP+; 24 (802.3af/at) PoE ports, 370 W budget; 176 Gbps switching capacity, 260 Mpps, 32 K MAC, <1 us latency, 4 K VLANs, 2 MB packet buffer, 512 MB DDR3, 64 MB flash, >10 years MTBF. 44 x 310 x 440 mm, 4.68 kg, side-to-back airflow. PoE is on ports 1-24 only - the front panel labels PoE Ports 1 to 24 with a PoE MAX LED of 370 W, so ports 25-48 are plain GE and are modelled unpowered (148F QuickStart Guide). FortiLink ports 45-52; SFP+ cages 49-52. Console RJ-45 at 115200 8-N-1 by default (https://docs.fortinet.com/document/fortiswitch/7.6.5/enterprise-data-center-switching-with-evpn-vxlan-deployment-guide/313313/deployment-procedures), console IP 192.168.1.99. Layer 2 only - the FortiGate routes over FortiLink. Same 370 W budget as the 124F-FPOE, but here it is spread over 24 PoE ports out of 48, not every port: ports 25-48 state poeOut 0 explicitly, because a PoE-capable switch gets every copper port promoted to a PSE by the engine when a port says nothing."
